course: dictionary
lesson: 4612
title: Hidden things and hidden meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Hidden is an adjective. It means put in a place where it cannot easily be seen or found. «The coloured paint marks are a map of that hidden city, showing where pipes and cables run.» The pipes are under the ground, so you cannot see them, but the paint shows where they are.
explain: Hidden can also mean secret, or not known by others. «A good secret, like a surprise party or a hidden present, ends happily.» Here nobody can see the present yet, so it is hidden from you until the surprise.
explain: Hidden is also a form of the verb hide: hide, hides, hid, hidden, hiding. Use the word «has» or «was» in front of it, as in «has hidden» or «was hidden». Check your meaning by swapping in a word like secret or out of sight. If it still makes sense, you have got it.
fact: Hidden is an adjective and also the past form of hide: hide, hides, hid, hidden, hiding.
fact: «Hidden» can mean put where it cannot easily be seen or found.
fact: «Hidden» can mean secret, as in a hidden meaning.
fact: Dangers can be hidden, such as a hidden step, ice under snow, or a hidden current in a river.
fact: Hidden treasure, hidden away and keep hidden all use this meaning.
exercise: «Stunt performers wear hidden safety gear.» What does hidden mean here? | Loud and bright | Taken away and lost forever | *Put where it cannot easily be seen | Very large and heavy
exercise: Mum warns, «The river has hidden currents.» What does hidden tell you about the currents? | They are the same as the sea | They are very slow and calm | They are bright and easy to spot | *You cannot easily see them, so they are dangerous
exercise: «A good secret, like a surprise party or a hidden present, ends happily.» Find and copy the word that means not known by others. | ends | happily | *hidden | good
test: «The workers spray paint on the pavement, a map of that hidden city.» What does hidden city mean? | A city that is very old and famous | A city that is painted blue | A city with lots of lights and cars | *A city under the ground that people cannot see
test: The cat has ___ under the bed. Choose the right word. | hide | hides | *hidden | hiding
exam: «Never swim near dams; the water has hidden currents.» What does this warning mean? | Currents that make the water bright | *Currents you cannot see, so they are dangerous | Currents that help you float | Currents that are warm and safe
